{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 41, :comments ["<b>And you were ready.</b> From the stem הן — that is to say, you said, 'Here we are, let us go up.' And the Targum rendered: ושריתון למיסק לטורא — 'and you prepared yourselves to go up to the mountain.' For one who readies himself for a matter, saying 'Here I am,' begins with it. And similarly (Psalms 88:16): נשאתי אימך אפונה — from the stem פן, that is to say, 'I have borne your fear, lest I be punished.'"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:44:43.914061143Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}